50: // PINS: journey-log chronology — the entries render newest-run-first and,
51: // inside one run, hop-ascending regardless of emission order; the ordering
52: // is the pure contract in model.js (orderJourneyEntries). The cap keeps the
53: // 20 newest entries (bottom tail trimmed), like the previous DOM trim, and
54: // the consecutive-emission dedupe (same label + text emitted twice in a row)
55: // stays: the duplicate frame is not logged (the render test pins ordering).
